{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 2642 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "40e8e7be633be89741ff6a2a3a39178028af7abb704b5f931bb57fc3167df41f" :edb/db-before-t 2641 :edb/db-after-t 2642 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535954 50 #inst "2026-10-09T11:31:08.117Z" 13194139535954 true] [17592186161925 1020 #edb/ref 17592186376233 13194139535954 true] [17592186161925 1020 #edb/ref 17592186376240 13194139535954 true] [17592186161925 1020 #edb/ref 17592186376247 13194139535954 true] [17592186162528 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535954 true] [17592186162528 1100 "Given that \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\n express the quadratic form $Q(x)={x}_{1}^{2}+3{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}$ in terms of the components of $y.$" 13194139535954 true] [17592186162528 1100 "Given that $\\begin{bmatrix}y_{1} \\\\ y_{2}\\end{bmatrix} = \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x_{1} \\\\ x_{2}\\end{bmatrix}$, express the quadratic form $Q(x) = x_{1}^{2} + 3x_{1}x_{2} + x_{2}^{2}$ in terms of the components of $y$." 13194139535954 false] [17592186162528 1145 "First, notice that \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\ngives the following expressions for ${y}_{1}$ and ${y}_{2}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} & ={x}_{1}+2{x}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{2} & =-{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBy solving the second equation for ${x}_{2}$ and substituting it into the first equation, we obtain the following expressions for ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & ={y}_{1}+2{y}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2} & =-{y}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute these into our quadratic form expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & ={x}_{1}^{2}+3{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =({y}_{1}+2{y}_{2})^{2}+3({y}_{1}+2{y}_{2})(-{y}_{2})+(-{y}_{2})^{2} \\\\  & ={y}_{1}^{2}+4{y}_{1}{y}_{2}+4{y}_{2}^{2}-3{y}_{1}{y}_{2}-6{y}_{2}^{2}+{y}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & ={y}_{1}^{2}+{y}_{1}{y}_{2}-{y}_{2}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535954 true] [17592186162547 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535954 true] [17592186162547 1100 "Given that \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\n express the quadratic form $Q(x)={x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{1}{x}_{2}-2{x}_{2}^{2}$ in terms of the components of $y.$" 13194139535954 true] [17592186162547 1100 "Given that $\\begin{bmatrix}y_{1} \\\\ y_{2}\\end{bmatrix} = \\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x_{1} \\\\ x_{2}\\end{bmatrix}$, express the quadratic form $Q(x) = x_{1}^{2} + x_{1}x_{2} - 2x_{2}^{2}$ in terms of the components of $y$." 13194139535954 false] [17592186162547 1145 "First, notice that \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\ngives the following expressions for ${y}_{1}$ and ${y}_{2}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} & ={x}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{2} & =-{x}_{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving these for ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =-{y}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2} & ={y}_{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute these into our quadratic form expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & ={x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{1}{x}_{2}-2{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =(-{y}_{2})^{2}+(-{y}_{2}){y}_{1}-2{y}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & ={y}_{2}^{2}-{y}_{2}{y}_{1}-2{y}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =-2{y}_{1}^{2}-{y}_{1}{y}_{2}+{y}_{2}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535954 true] [17592186376233 1017 #edb/ref 17592186376234 13194139535954 true] [17592186376233 1089 "q-94182" 13194139535954 true] [17592186376233 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535954 true] [17592186376233 1100 "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,P=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrices $A$ and $P$ above. Find the matrix of the quadratic form ${x}^{T}\\,Ax$ in the basis that consists of the columns of $P.$" 13194139535954 true] [17592186376233 1113 #uuid "89a8b501-1e1d-5651-8ffd-47612aef6ccf" 13194139535954 true] [17592186376233 1145 "Recall that if $x=[{x}_{1},{x}_{2}]^{T}$ is a vector given by its coordinates in the standard basis and $y=[{y}_{1},{y}_{2}]^{T}$ is the same vector but given in the coordinates relative to the basis that consists of the columns of $P,$ then \n\n$$\nx=Py.\n$$\n\nAs a result, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{T}\\,Ax & =(Py)^{T}\\,A\\,(Py) \\\\  & =({y}^{T}{P}^{T})\\,A\\,(Py) \\\\  & ={y}^{T}({P}^{T}\\,AP)\\,y,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich means that the matrix of our form in the new basis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}^{T}\\,AP & ={[\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]}^{T}[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}8 & 5 \\\\ 10 & 6\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}21 & 26 \\\\ 26 & 32\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535954 true] [17592186376234 1000 #edb/ref 17592186376235 13194139535954 true] [17592186376234 1000 #edb/ref 17592186376236 13194139535954 true] [17592186376234 1000 #edb/ref 17592186376237 13194139535954 true] [17592186376234 1000 #edb/ref 17592186376238 13194139535954 true] [17592186376234 1000 #edb/ref 17592186376239 13194139535954 true] [17592186376234 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535954 true] [17592186376234 1041 "selection" 13194139535954 true] [17592186376234 1104 #edb/ref 17592186376238 13194139535954 true] [17592186376234 1110 #uuid "720abd7a-75d5-567c-827e-a8a90b77fa21" 13194139535954 true] [17592186